{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Seeing you are his wife.</b> That is, it is not that he withheld you from me for any trivial reason, but rather it is precisely the fact that you are his wife that is what withholds you from me. Or it may be said to remove the aspect of merit [that she might claim]." "<b>And how could I do</b> etc. That is, for by this I would lose all the good that I have attained." "<b>Moreover,</b> I would deprive myself of the source of souls, for this thing is forbidden even to the children of Noah, and that is what he meant by ״וְחָטָאתִי לֵאלֹהִים״." "<b>Furthermore,</b> it may intend that she cannot argue that I would hide the matter so that his master would not know, and thus he would remain in his position without any loss. Therefore he said ״וְחָטָאתִי לֵאלֹהִים״ — for He is the one who placed me in this position, and from Him nothing is hidden, and so it turns out I would be losing my good position."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The phrase 'לְצַד שֶׁאַתְּ אִשְׁתּוֹ' is read as the reason for withholding; the final clause 'אוֹ לִשְׁלוֹל צַד הַמַּעֲלָה' is terse and I render it hyper-literally; it may intend 'or to negate any grounds for her claim of merit.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:05.956230012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}